-# S002 Review and confirm
+# Story: Review and confirm extracted proposals
 
-TODO
+**Story ID**: `S002-review-confirm` &nbsp;·&nbsp; **Qualified**: `E001/S002`
+**Created**: 2026-08-11
+**Status**: Specified
+**Current State**: Specified
+**Input**: Complete S002 as a canonical story specification.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Experience (What the user lives)
+
+### 1a. JTBD Context
+
+**When** an upload has produced proposed actions, the operations-user wants to review each proposal and explicitly confirm the set to schedule, **so that** only human-approved actions move from capture into scheduling.
+
+Cross-reference: no project-level product contract is present in this workspace. This story deliberately claims no `MM-N` or `JOB-N` promise until that contract exists.
+
+### 1b. Primary User Story
+
+As an operations-user, I want to review extracted action proposals and confirm the ones I accept so that scheduling receives a deliberate, human-approved set of actions.
+
+### 1c. Felt Quality (How the user feels)
+
+| Surface | Entry emotional state | Target felt outcome | Banned feelings |
+|---------|----------------------|--------------------|-----------------|
+| Proposal review | Cautious about automated extraction | In control: each proposal is readable and the approval boundary is obvious | Confusion, pressure, surprise |
+| Confirmation result | Ready to hand work forward | Certain that only the chosen proposals can be scheduled | Ambiguity, accidental commitment |
+
+### 1d. Magic Moments Tied to This Story
+
+No magic moments are claimed: `serves: []`. The workspace has no `product-contract.md` from which valid `MM-N` identifiers could be derived.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Acceptance LARP (How we prove the experience works)
+
+### 2a. Required Personas to LARP
+
+| Persona | Flow | Build artifact | Evidence required |
+|---------|------|----------------|-------------------|
+| operations-user | Review proposals produced by S001, select accepted proposals, and confirm | Running application review surface | Screenshot, accessibility tree, and interaction transcript |
+
+### 2b. Acceptance Scenarios
+
+#### AC-1 — Review proposed actions before confirmation
+- **GIVEN** the running application contains a completed S001 capture with one or more extracted action proposals that have not been confirmed
+- **WHEN** the operations-user opens that capture for review
+- **THEN** the application SHALL show each proposal in a reviewable state and SHALL distinguish proposals that are not yet confirmed from actions eligible for scheduling
+- **AND** the application SHALL provide a clear way to select the proposals the user accepts
+- **EVIDENCE** `screenshots/<sha>-review-proposals.png`, `ax-trees/<sha>-review-proposals.txt`, and `larp-recordings/<sha>-operations-user-review.md`
+- **VERIFIABILITY** agent-LARP
+
+#### AC-2 — Confirm the selected proposal set
+- **GIVEN** the operations-user is reviewing an S001 capture and has selected at least one proposal
+- **WHEN** the operations-user invokes the confirmation action
+- **THEN** the application SHALL present an explicit confirmation outcome for the selected proposals
+- **AND** the confirmed proposals SHALL become the only proposals from that review eligible for S003 scheduling
+- **EVIDENCE** `screenshots/<sha>-confirmation-result.png`, `ax-trees/<sha>-confirmation-result.txt`, and `larp-recordings/<sha>-operations-user-confirm.md`
+- **VERIFIABILITY** agent-LARP
+
+#### AC-3 — Avoid accidental confirmation when no proposal is selected
+- **GIVEN** the operations-user is reviewing an S001 capture with no proposals selected
+- **WHEN** the operations-user attempts to confirm
+- **THEN** the application SHALL not mark any proposal as confirmed
+- **AND** the application SHALL make the required selection clear without losing the review state
+- **EVIDENCE** `screenshots/<sha>-empty-confirmation-attempt.png`, `ax-trees/<sha>-empty-confirmation-attempt.txt`, and `larp-recordings/<sha>-operations-user-empty-selection.md`
+- **VERIFIABILITY** agent-LARP
+
+---
+
+## 3. Evidence Required
+
+| Evidence type | Required for state | Verifiable by | Path / convention |
+|---------------|--------------------|---------------|-------------------|
+| Primary review screenshot | UX-RC | agent-LARP | `screenshots/<sha>-review-proposals.png` |
+| Confirmation-result screenshot | UX-RC | agent-LARP | `screenshots/<sha>-confirmation-result.png` |
+| Accessibility trees for review and empty-selection states | UX-RC | agent-LARP | `ax-trees/<sha>-*.txt` |
+| Operations-user interaction transcripts | UX-RC | agent-LARP | `larp-recordings/<sha>-operations-user-*.md` |
+| Adversarial results for confirmation boundaries | SHIP-RC | agent-LARP | `audit-report.md` |
+
+---
+
+## 4. Adversarial Cases (What must NOT happen)
+
+| Condition | Must NOT happen | Probe used to verify |
+|-----------|-----------------|----------------------|
+| A proposal has not been selected | It becomes confirmed or schedule-eligible | Attempt confirmation with no selection; inspect proposal state and S003 eligibility |
+| A proposal was not extracted by S001 | It appears as a reviewable proposal for this capture | Load a capture fixture with no matching extracted proposal and inspect the review list |
+| Confirmation request fails | The UI reports success or leaves an uncertain confirmed state | Inject a confirmation failure and verify an explicit recoverable result with no newly eligible action |
+| User repeats the confirm action | Duplicate confirmed actions are created | Trigger confirmation twice and assert one confirmed representation per selected proposal |
+| Review surface is dismissed or refreshed | Unconfirmed proposals silently become confirmed | Reopen the capture and inspect its confirmation state |
+
+---
+
+## 5. Failure-Modes Handled
+
+| Dependency | Failure mode | Behavior | Verified by |
+|------------|--------------|----------|-------------|
+| S001 proposal source | Capture has no extracted proposals | The review surface communicates that there is nothing to confirm and exposes no false confirmation success | AC-3 LARP with an empty proposal fixture |
+| Confirmation persistence | Save request fails | No proposal becomes schedule-eligible; the user receives a clear failure result and can retry from the preserved review state | Failure-injection LARP and integration test |
+| Review data load | Proposals cannot be loaded | The user sees a recoverable load failure rather than a blank list that could be mistaken for no proposals | Failure-injection LARP |
+
+---
+
+## 6. Related Tables / Surfaces (Cascade)
+
+| Write target | Related tables | Cascade behavior | Verified |
+|--------------|----------------|------------------|----------|
+| Proposal confirmation state | S001 capture/review surface; S003 scheduling input | Confirmation makes only the selected proposals available to S003; unselected proposals remain unavailable | AC-2 interaction transcript plus integration test |
+
+No concrete data-table names are asserted because the workspace contains no domain model or implementation. `plan.md` may name the actual persistence surfaces after the implementation context is examined.
+
+---
+
+## 7. Performance + Non-Functional Targets
+
+- Performance: The review surface makes the loaded proposal set and its confirmation affordance available without avoidable blocking work; a numeric target is deferred to `context.md`, which is absent.
+- Accessibility: WCAG 2.1 AA; proposal state, selection state, and confirmation feedback are programmatically determinable.
+- Security/privacy: Only proposals belonging to the selected capture may be reviewed or confirmed; authorization details remain an implementation concern for `plan.md`.
+- Observability: Record confirmation success and failure with the capture and proposal identifiers needed to diagnose an incorrect eligibility transition, without logging proposal content unnecessarily.
+
+---
+
+## 8. Data + API (Last, not first)
+
+### Key Entities
+- **Extracted proposal**: A candidate action created by S001 and awaiting human review.
+- **Confirmation state**: The user’s explicit decision that determines whether an extracted proposal is eligible for S003 scheduling.
+
+### API Surface
+- **Review/confirmation interface**: Loads proposals for one completed capture and records a single explicit confirmation decision for the selected proposals. Concrete endpoint and payload choices belong in `plan.md`.
+
+---
+
+## 9. Implementation Hint (Optional)
+
+Preserve the distinction between extracted, selected, and confirmed states. S003 must consume confirmed proposals only.
+
